WEBVTT

00:05.370 --> 00:07.210
Good morning.

00:10.400 --> 00:12.050
Morning...

00:13.780 --> 00:15.710
It's a lovely day outside.

00:16.530 --> 00:18.410
It sure is.

00:18.410 --> 00:21.540
Pochi, what's my schedule for today?

00:21.540 --> 00:24.320
You're free to do as you want until noon.

00:24.320 --> 00:27.220
Pontaro-san will be joining you for lunch.

00:27.540 --> 00:29.310
Pontaro...

00:29.310 --> 00:31.320
Okay, got it.

00:31.320 --> 00:32.960
No one else is coming over?

00:33.350 --> 00:34.040
Correct.

00:34.040 --> 00:36.470
No one will come here, so rest assured.

00:36.940 --> 00:38.480
I see.

00:38.480 --> 00:39.930
Let's have breakfast.

00:39.930 --> 00:42.150
I need to leave for school at 8:30.

00:42.150 --> 00:43.320
Understood.

00:43.320 --> 00:46.470
Please change into these first, then.

00:47.280 --> 00:49.230
Did I do my homework?

00:49.230 --> 00:50.340
You did.

00:50.340 --> 00:51.750
Really?

00:51.750 --> 00:53.250
Thanks, Pochi.

00:53.250 --> 00:53.920
You're welcome.

00:56.820 --> 00:58.450
Time to eat.

00:58.450 --> 00:59.380
Go on.

01:03.370 --> 01:06.330
<b>Study Hall</b>

01:06.330 --> 01:09.790
<b>Study Hall</b>

01:37.280 --> 01:41.030
<b>Train to the End of the World</b>

02:55.750 --> 02:57.440
Oh, Yoka-hime!

02:57.440 --> 03:01.460
I see you're looking healthier, 
cooler, and sexier than ever.

03:01.460 --> 03:02.320
Hello.

03:02.320 --> 03:05.510
To think you'd greet a humble 
servant such as myself!

03:05.510 --> 03:07.660
I, Poison Pontaro, am overcome with joy.

03:07.660 --> 03:10.810
Which is to say, I'm honored beyond words!

03:10.810 --> 03:12.930
What's for lunch?

03:12.930 --> 03:17.420
Ten-times-spicy curry with 
an Agano bitter melon salad in vinegar.

03:17.970 --> 03:19.290
Agano...

03:19.290 --> 03:22.920
This rural menu might not be 
to Yoka-hime's taste!

03:22.920 --> 03:25.390
In other words, make her something different!

03:25.390 --> 03:26.260
Pronto!

03:26.260 --> 03:27.910
Bitter melon's fine.

03:27.910 --> 03:29.480
But why bitter melon?

03:29.480 --> 03:31.440
We got some in stock through Hoya.

03:31.440 --> 03:33.950
It seems it was brought in via caravan.

03:33.950 --> 03:35.020
Huh...

03:39.140 --> 03:40.270
Agano...

03:40.840 --> 03:42.580
Well, well, well!

03:42.580 --> 03:44.270
Pochi-kun, thanks for all your hard work!

03:44.270 --> 03:46.810
"Pochi-kun" begins with a "Po," 
just like the humble "Pontaro."

03:46.810 --> 03:50.670
As fellow "Po"s, we should both serve 
the princess with the utmost loyalty!

03:50.670 --> 03:51.790
That is what I strive to do.

03:52.930 --> 03:56.730
Sheesh, Pochicchi, you only 
ever think about the princess!

03:56.730 --> 03:58.030
How cute!

03:58.030 --> 03:59.170
You want to eat, too?

03:59.170 --> 04:00.370
Yes, of course.

04:00.370 --> 04:01.420
Yes, yes!

04:02.640 --> 04:04.550
Time to dig in!

04:06.250 --> 04:07.840
Um...

04:07.840 --> 04:09.570
Gontaro-san?

04:09.570 --> 04:11.170
It's Pontaro, but yes?

04:11.170 --> 04:13.410
Tontaro-san, who are you again?

04:13.410 --> 04:14.020
Excuse me?

04:14.020 --> 04:16.240
You come over to hang out a lot.

04:16.240 --> 04:17.670
I was wondering why, exactly.

04:17.670 --> 04:19.680
Oh, come now!

04:19.680 --> 04:21.790
Surely you jest, Princess!

04:21.790 --> 04:23.910
To think you'd forget your loyal subject.

04:23.910 --> 04:26.120
I'm Poison Pontaro, the mayor.

04:26.120 --> 04:27.570
Please do try and remember!

04:27.850 --> 04:30.180
You're going on about 
princesses and subjects,

04:30.180 --> 04:31.890
but I don't really get what you mean.

04:31.890 --> 04:32.780
I'm no—

04:32.290 --> 04:34.020
What are you saying?!

04:34.020 --> 04:35.010
Have you forgotten?

04:35.010 --> 04:37.310
The day you came to Ikebukuro,

04:37.310 --> 04:40.090
which is to say, the day Ikebukuro 
welcomed you as our princess—

04:40.090 --> 04:43.090
When I came to Ikebukuro...

04:43.090 --> 04:46.610
—the one who greeted you was none 
other than myself, Pontaro!

04:46.610 --> 04:47.400
You don't remember?

04:47.400 --> 04:48.900
How tragic!

04:48.900 --> 04:52.110
If I may put it in more 
specialized terminology,

04:52.110 --> 04:54.380
it truly is so sad!

05:00.230 --> 05:01.540
That girl did?

05:01.540 --> 05:02.670
There's no mistaking it.

05:02.670 --> 05:04.270
She became the trigger, all right.

05:04.270 --> 05:06.570
Her personal effects suggest 
her name is Nakatomi Yoka.

05:05.360 --> 05:10.410
Episode 9       More Boring Than I Thought

05:06.570 --> 05:08.770
A high school girl living in Agano.

05:08.770 --> 05:12.270
Seeing how it turned out, we'd have been 
better off heeding those warnings.

05:12.270 --> 05:12.890
Hey, now.

05:12.890 --> 05:15.230
Let's stick to the story that 
everything went as planned.

05:15.230 --> 05:18.420
No matter what, it's too late 
to say that 7G was a failure.

05:18.420 --> 05:19.960
How do we change it all back?

05:19.960 --> 05:21.140
Hey, hey, hey, hey.

05:21.140 --> 05:22.820
No way we're taking the blame.

05:22.820 --> 05:24.640
We'll play dumb and keep things as they are.

05:24.640 --> 05:25.930
No one knows what went on here.

05:25.930 --> 05:27.840
Well, one person does, 
but his brain's mush now.

05:27.840 --> 05:29.860
All we need to do now 
is handle things with her.

05:29.860 --> 05:30.380
Listen up.

05:30.380 --> 05:32.060
Don't ever let her out of your sight.

05:32.060 --> 05:33.130
Understood.

05:33.130 --> 05:35.910
Slip up in any way, and no more chow for you!

05:36.310 --> 05:38.470
Good morning.

05:38.470 --> 05:39.710
Morning.

05:40.130 --> 05:41.290
Huh?

05:41.290 --> 05:44.000
What was I doing, again?

05:44.000 --> 05:45.940
Everything's a blur.

05:48.370 --> 05:50.110
I think it's about time we got up.

05:50.580 --> 05:51.980
Why?

05:51.980 --> 05:54.200
We need to go for a walk.

05:54.200 --> 05:57.210
I was told that it's important to poop.

05:57.770 --> 06:00.390
Hurry and wake up.

06:00.390 --> 06:02.090
Let's go for a walk.

06:04.470 --> 06:05.980
You remind me of Pochi-san.

06:05.980 --> 06:06.910
"Pochi"?

06:06.910 --> 06:11.510
My big dog who loves walks 
and is always by my side.

06:11.840 --> 06:13.840
Not to mention how strong and kind he is.

06:13.840 --> 06:15.270
Is that so?

06:15.270 --> 06:18.430
Then please, call me Pochi.

06:18.430 --> 06:20.180
I'll always be at your side.

06:20.500 --> 06:22.630
I've taken on a large body now.

06:22.630 --> 06:24.310
It's most likely strong.

06:24.310 --> 06:28.640
I may find it difficult now 
to jump as high as before,

06:28.640 --> 06:31.010
but that shouldn't pose much of a problem.

06:31.010 --> 06:32.270
But you're...

06:32.270 --> 06:33.800
I'm Pochi.

06:33.800 --> 06:35.460
Let's go for a walk.

06:37.350 --> 06:38.990
So this is Ikebukuro?

06:38.990 --> 06:40.540
It appears so.

06:40.850 --> 06:42.400
Really?

06:42.400 --> 06:45.950
It's different from what I was expecting.

06:45.950 --> 06:47.400
Apparently it's like this now.

06:47.400 --> 06:51.750
I'm not sure whether it's more amazing 
or more boring than I thought.

06:51.750 --> 06:55.110
It might become a more 
bustling place in the future.

06:55.110 --> 06:55.840
More bustling?

06:55.840 --> 06:56.740
Yes.

06:56.740 --> 07:00.870
After all, you're here 
in Ikebukuro, Yoka-sama.

07:04.840 --> 07:06.090
That seems unrelated.

07:06.090 --> 07:07.560
I hear otherwise.

07:07.560 --> 07:11.450
The current Ikebukuro is deeply 
related to you, Yoka-sama.

07:11.450 --> 07:12.430
You have a point.

07:12.430 --> 07:15.430
It'd be better if it were 
bustling instead of desolate.

07:15.430 --> 07:16.400
That's right.

07:16.660 --> 07:20.100
While we're at it, taller and bigger, too.

07:22.670 --> 07:25.770
With a less distant, more beautiful sky.

07:27.020 --> 07:29.450
The city sure is nice.

07:29.450 --> 07:31.250
You feel better when everything's so lively.

07:31.540 --> 07:33.760
Do you feel bad when it's quiet?

07:35.220 --> 07:37.300
When it's quiet...

07:37.300 --> 07:39.630
When something happens, and it's quiet...

07:39.630 --> 07:41.220
I don't know if I feel bad, exactly.

07:41.220 --> 07:42.960
I'm fine with it being quiet, but...

07:42.960 --> 07:46.980
Um, let me think...

07:50.380 --> 07:52.870
Anyway, the city's nice, too.

07:52.870 --> 07:54.020
Yes, I agree.

07:54.370 --> 07:59.270
The other day, I made my men go search 
the Shibuya, Shinjuku, and Ueno areas,

07:59.270 --> 08:00.940
but they were nowhere to be found.

08:00.940 --> 08:02.580
Huh, that's rough.

08:02.580 --> 08:05.180
However, thanks to your authority,

08:05.180 --> 08:07.750
Ikebukuro is in great shape, 
with everything going smoothly!

08:07.750 --> 08:08.650
Dark matter.

08:08.650 --> 08:09.170
What?

08:09.170 --> 08:11.130
Did they ever find any?

08:11.130 --> 08:12.200
Eh...

08:12.200 --> 08:12.840
Pochi?

08:12.840 --> 08:16.590
It's neutrinos that they say 
have been detected.

08:16.590 --> 08:19.260
I thought those weren't dark matter.

08:19.260 --> 08:20.760
Who was it that discovered them?

08:20.760 --> 08:22.200
Oh, that's right.

08:22.200 --> 08:23.670
The one who likes video games.

08:23.670 --> 08:24.440
"Games"?

08:24.800 --> 08:25.910
Video games.

08:28.100 --> 08:29.560
Games aside...

08:29.560 --> 08:30.120
Princess!

08:30.120 --> 08:33.130
There are intruders in Ikebukuro 
who bear a grudge against you!

08:33.130 --> 08:33.990
Bear a grudge?

08:34.300 --> 08:35.430
That's right!

08:35.430 --> 08:38.940
They harp on about how the world's 
gone weird and crazy or whatnot!

08:40.020 --> 08:41.740
There you are, foul witch!

08:41.740 --> 08:43.830
Bring back the world that disappeared!

08:43.830 --> 08:45.070
Bring it back?

08:45.070 --> 08:46.530
I don't really understand.

08:46.530 --> 08:48.830
You've gone and erased everything!

08:48.830 --> 08:50.420
Me? I erased it?

08:50.420 --> 08:50.790
Why?

08:50.790 --> 08:51.820
Don't play dumb!

08:51.820 --> 08:54.710
Thanks to you and that 
7G incident you brought about,

08:54.710 --> 08:56.460
the world's gotten all messed up!

08:56.770 --> 08:59.050
Do you hate this world?

08:59.050 --> 09:00.770
It's not a matter of love or hate!

09:00.770 --> 09:02.810
But you think it's messed up, right?

09:03.730 --> 09:05.410
What utter disrespect!

09:05.410 --> 09:08.070
You dare go against the 
authority of the princess?

09:07.440 --> 09:08.540
Shut up!

09:08.540 --> 09:11.910
Why must the other train lines 
be sacrificed?!

09:13.230 --> 09:14.340
You're wrong.

09:14.340 --> 09:16.290
Nothing's been sacrificed.

09:16.290 --> 09:17.740
It's always been this way.

09:17.740 --> 09:19.400
And it always will be, too.

09:19.400 --> 09:21.630
To hell with this way!

09:21.630 --> 09:23.430
Bring back the old world!

09:23.430 --> 09:25.820
I know nothing about the world you mean.

09:25.050 --> 09:26.250
That's right!

09:26.250 --> 09:27.470
It doesn't exist! It can't!

09:27.470 --> 09:30.000
I know about your powers!

09:30.000 --> 09:31.640
Witch of Ikebukuro!

09:31.640 --> 09:34.500
The Ikebukuro you've created 
is nothing but a sham!

09:34.500 --> 09:35.620
Liar...

09:35.620 --> 09:36.680
That's right!

09:36.680 --> 09:38.870
These people are simply delusional!

09:38.870 --> 09:41.320
This old world of theirs never existed!

09:41.320 --> 09:44.790
And even if it did, to blame 
the princess of all people...

09:44.790 --> 09:46.640
Oh! Oh, my!

09:46.640 --> 09:48.810
This reeks of a conspiracy!

09:48.810 --> 09:50.070
Unforgivable!

09:56.940 --> 09:59.260
Serves you right, you no-good egg custard!

09:59.260 --> 10:01.010
This is what you get for defying the princess!

10:01.010 --> 10:02.880
Which is to say, 
die while you're steaming hot!

10:02.880 --> 10:03.590
Hot, hot!

10:03.590 --> 10:04.620
You sure are damn hot!

10:04.620 --> 10:06.710
Aw, man. I ate another one.

10:06.060 --> 10:07.360
Let us go back.

10:07.360 --> 10:09.460
It's quite windy here.

10:11.290 --> 10:14.720
Why did that man hate this world?

10:14.720 --> 10:15.800
I couldn't say.

10:15.800 --> 10:16.830
It's fun, right?

10:16.830 --> 10:21.200
If you think it's fun, 
then I, too, find it fun.

10:21.200 --> 10:23.700
Is it really fun?

10:23.700 --> 10:26.450
What does it mean to be fun?

10:26.450 --> 10:28.720
Pochi, can I have a word with you?

10:29.720 --> 10:32.830
I don't like that Montaro or whoever.

10:32.830 --> 10:34.560
I'll be right back.

10:34.920 --> 10:38.240
Don't you forget who you're in debt to.

10:38.240 --> 10:40.330
You nameless, blockheaded dumbbell.

10:40.330 --> 10:44.040
Without me, you'd just be 
a member of the loser club.

10:44.040 --> 10:45.580
Is that all you had to say to me?

10:45.910 --> 10:47.450
Do your job!

10:47.450 --> 10:50.170
She gets weirdly emotionally unstable lately!

10:50.170 --> 10:54.230
If you notice anything out of the ordinary, 
let me know right away!

10:54.230 --> 10:55.340
I understand.

10:55.340 --> 10:57.310
Do you really?!

10:57.310 --> 10:59.090
If you do anything to betray me,

10:59.090 --> 11:01.170
you'll <i>wish</i> you got turned into egg custard!

11:06.960 --> 11:09.550
This doesn't feel like the 
Ikebukuro line at all.

11:09.550 --> 11:11.000
You're only saying this now?

11:11.000 --> 11:15.090
I bet Mom and Dad would be real 
surprised if they could see all this.

11:15.090 --> 11:16.030
You think?

11:16.030 --> 11:18.470
They might just go, "Huh..."

11:18.770 --> 11:24.250
Reimi, your dad's a naked mole-rat, 
and your mom's a tree-kangaroo, right?

11:24.250 --> 11:25.880
Yeah. And Grandpa's a trilobite.

11:25.880 --> 11:27.200
Oh, shoot!

11:27.200 --> 11:29.280
I forgot to return my books to the library.

11:29.280 --> 11:30.340
You'll get a fine.

11:30.340 --> 11:32.200
I bet they're just more weird books.

11:32.200 --> 11:33.980
It's all right. No one's borrowing those.

11:33.980 --> 11:35.420
No, it's not, Reimi-chan!

11:35.420 --> 11:36.760
That's not the issue.

11:36.760 --> 11:38.030
This is bad...

11:38.030 --> 11:39.480
See, Shizuru-chan agrees.

11:39.480 --> 11:42.910
I feel like I left my lunch box 
behind half-eaten.

11:42.910 --> 11:43.630
What?!

11:43.630 --> 11:48.070
I think on top of my bed, or inside...

11:46.660 --> 11:47.880
Ugh!

11:47.880 --> 11:49.370
What do you mean, "inside"?

11:49.370 --> 11:51.300
Well, I just...

11:51.300 --> 11:53.650
I'm sure your mom took care of it!

11:53.650 --> 11:54.190
Yeah, yeah.

11:54.190 --> 11:56.830
Don't red pandas wash 
their hands before eating?

11:56.830 --> 11:58.600
You're thinking of raccoons.

11:58.600 --> 11:59.120
Huh?

11:59.120 --> 12:00.690
So red pandas don't wash themselves?

12:00.690 --> 12:03.930
She always washes the dishes 
after cooking and stuff.

12:03.930 --> 12:05.060
Then it's fine.

12:05.060 --> 12:06.520
What's with that optimism?

12:06.520 --> 12:07.800
You think that's overly positive?

12:07.800 --> 12:10.070
Akira, didn't you say 
her mom would handle it?

12:10.070 --> 12:11.480
I mean, yeah...

12:10.700 --> 12:13.240
Someone'll take care of it...

12:14.100 --> 12:16.290
Thanks for coming along with me!

12:16.570 --> 12:18.050
What's this, out of the blue?

12:18.050 --> 12:19.670
Don't scare me like that!

12:19.670 --> 12:21.620
Oh, just felt like it.

12:21.620 --> 12:23.230
We didn't just tag along.

12:23.600 --> 12:25.730
We came because we wanted to.

12:25.730 --> 12:27.410
Yeah, it's been pretty fun.

12:27.410 --> 12:28.240
Once we get back,

12:28.240 --> 12:31.980
I'll need to write a travelogue before 
I turn 21 years and three months old.

12:31.980 --> 12:33.220
Oh, I'll totally read it!

12:33.220 --> 12:34.760
Wait, I'll be in it, right?

12:34.760 --> 12:36.170
I guess you'll have to be.

12:36.170 --> 12:37.840
Make me real awesome in it!

12:37.840 --> 12:40.110
The strong, beautiful, and smart Reimi-chan!

12:40.110 --> 12:40.680
Nuh-uh.

12:40.680 --> 12:42.240
I need to put down the truth.

12:42.240 --> 12:44.320
What do you mean? It's all true!

12:44.320 --> 12:47.650
Well, we don't know if we'll 
even make it back to Agano.

12:48.380 --> 12:50.430
You mean we might end up 
staying in Ikebukuro?

12:50.430 --> 12:51.740
Nah, probably not.

12:51.740 --> 12:52.720
No way!

12:53.080 --> 12:55.830
Well, I guess it's possible.

12:55.830 --> 12:56.570
What?

12:56.570 --> 12:58.760
We need to go back with Yoka-chan!

12:58.760 --> 12:59.830
Everyone's waiting back home.

12:59.830 --> 13:01.050
That's true.

13:01.050 --> 13:02.400
Are they really?

13:02.400 --> 13:02.800
Huh?

13:08.090 --> 13:09.650
What's that?

13:13.350 --> 13:15.210
The hermit! In the swan boat!

13:15.210 --> 13:16.340
The old man who gave us the map?

13:16.340 --> 13:17.510
That shady guy!

13:17.510 --> 13:18.410
Hey, look!

13:19.300 --> 13:20.330
Isn't he in trouble?

13:20.330 --> 13:21.050
Do we leave him be?

13:21.050 --> 13:21.860
No way, no way!

13:27.130 --> 13:29.230
We need something to...

13:29.230 --> 13:30.330
Out of the way, you two!

13:30.330 --> 13:30.880
What?

13:30.880 --> 13:32.290
Reimi-chan, bring the rope!

13:32.290 --> 13:33.410
Huh? Okay!

13:33.410 --> 13:34.660
What now, Nadeko-chan?

13:34.660 --> 13:36.220
Stop the train, Shizuru-chan!

13:36.220 --> 13:37.170
Okay!

13:44.970 --> 13:46.670
Help me!

13:46.670 --> 13:47.710
Land!

13:53.930 --> 13:56.520
Good golly, I thought I was dead.

13:56.520 --> 13:59.590
Weren't you going up the Ikebukuro line?

13:59.590 --> 14:00.870
Why'd you come from Ikebukuro?

14:00.870 --> 14:03.400
No, I had passed Agano,

14:03.400 --> 14:07.700
and was heading deeper and deeper west 
in hopes of reaching Nishi-Agano.

14:07.700 --> 14:08.540
Huh?

14:08.540 --> 14:10.520
But you came from Ikebukuro's direction.

14:10.520 --> 14:12.520
Did you make a wide turn somewhere?

14:12.520 --> 14:14.270
There's absolutely...

14:14.270 --> 14:15.930
a possibility that happened.

14:15.930 --> 14:17.040
What the heck?

14:17.360 --> 14:19.010
Let me see the map.

14:19.010 --> 14:21.270
The one I gave you last time.

14:22.000 --> 14:23.170
Where'd we put it?

14:23.170 --> 14:24.040
Beats me.

14:24.340 --> 14:25.010
Here it is.

14:25.010 --> 14:27.490
Can't you treat it with more care?!

14:26.500 --> 14:29.440
Everything on it is way too vague!

14:29.440 --> 14:30.620
It's like heta-uma anti-art.

14:30.620 --> 14:35.010
This map is the only one that shows 
the condition of the world today!

14:35.010 --> 14:36.180
It's a nugget of wisdom!

14:36.180 --> 14:37.860
Do you remember?

14:37.860 --> 14:39.560
We first met here!

14:39.560 --> 14:40.900
And now we're here.

14:41.930 --> 14:43.720
Is that so?

14:43.720 --> 14:44.120
Huh?

14:44.120 --> 14:47.270
Is this mushroom for Higashi-Agano?

14:47.270 --> 14:47.760
Huh?

14:47.760 --> 14:50.070
And this is Musashi-Yokote's goat people?

14:50.070 --> 14:52.800
These are... the tiny people of Inariyama?

14:52.800 --> 14:54.700
This one seems like a 
really long shot, but...

14:54.700 --> 14:55.800
Chaos from <i>NeriAli</i>?

14:55.800 --> 14:57.740
So this map was right all along?

14:57.740 --> 14:58.700
Didn't I just say?

14:58.700 --> 14:59.940
It's a nugget of wisdom.

14:59.940 --> 15:05.100
Who'd think a guy meandering about in a 
swan boat would know all about these places?

15:05.100 --> 15:11.170
How do you think humans learned about 
galaxies 13.4 billion light years away?

15:11.170 --> 15:12.480
No idea.

15:12.480 --> 15:14.640
An inquisitive mind, I say!

15:14.640 --> 15:16.750
And the ability to calmly observe.

15:16.750 --> 15:17.450
I see...

15:17.450 --> 15:21.550
My inquisition drove me to devote myself 
to journeying up the Koma River.

15:21.550 --> 15:23.610
Ah, I think you mentioned that.

15:23.610 --> 15:26.600
And for whatever reason, we now 
find ourselves reunited here.

15:26.600 --> 15:28.410
What an intriguing phenomenon!

15:28.410 --> 15:30.700
Are you sure you didn't turn back 
without realizing it?

15:30.700 --> 15:33.380
Oh, yeah. People like that 
forget what they did all the time.

15:33.380 --> 15:35.060
Your brain goes senile as you get old.

15:35.060 --> 15:35.870
That's not it!

15:35.870 --> 15:38.180
There's nothing abnormal with my brain!

15:38.180 --> 15:41.880
If there's anything abnormal here, 
it's the world we live in!

15:41.880 --> 15:44.770
Ah, you think I'm just 
pointing out the obvious.

15:44.770 --> 15:48.140
Mushrooms, pseudo-giants, zombies, 
and the now-mighty Koma River!

15:48.140 --> 15:50.630
It's true that the world has changed greatly.

15:50.630 --> 15:53.870
But I'm talking about the changes 
that are still happening as we speak!

15:53.870 --> 15:56.120
Um, what do you mean, still happening?

15:56.120 --> 15:58.970
The world is contracting, 
Ikebukuro is expanding,

15:58.970 --> 16:01.500
and the rules governing the world 
grow ever more turbulent!

16:01.500 --> 16:03.970
All this difficult stuff is going 
right over my head...

16:03.970 --> 16:06.230
By expanding, is that a figure 
of speech for prosperity?

16:06.230 --> 16:07.850
No, it's literally expanding!

16:07.850 --> 16:10.260
Ikebukuro is swelling up 
like a fleshy balloon!

16:10.260 --> 16:12.130
That's a real gross image.

16:12.130 --> 16:14.050
What will happen after all that swelling?

16:14.050 --> 16:14.930
It'll disappear.

16:15.430 --> 16:17.800
You mean Ikebukuro? Agano?

16:17.800 --> 16:19.210
It'll all disappear.

16:19.210 --> 16:20.480
Can't we stop it?

16:20.480 --> 16:21.110
Nope!

16:21.110 --> 16:21.900
You're certain?

16:21.900 --> 16:22.900
That's the facts.

16:22.900 --> 16:24.190
Hold on a sec.

16:24.190 --> 16:26.330
The city has leaders and stuff, right?

16:26.330 --> 16:28.080
Why don't they do anything?

16:28.080 --> 16:30.370
Do they not exist?

16:30.370 --> 16:31.960
I never thought about it.

16:31.960 --> 16:34.170
You really need to think about this stuff.

16:34.170 --> 16:34.980
It's no use.

16:34.980 --> 16:37.880
If they felt like doing anything, 
they'd have done it by now.

16:37.880 --> 16:39.300
Yeah, that's true.

16:39.300 --> 16:42.060
Looks like all we can do is take 
matters into our own hands.

16:42.060 --> 16:43.230
I don't know about that.

16:43.230 --> 16:43.650
What?

16:43.910 --> 16:48.340
I can't help but feel that 
there are powers in Ikebukuro

16:48.340 --> 16:51.140
trying to stop those 
who would fix this disordered world.

16:51.140 --> 16:57.130
If you head to Ikebukuro, you might have 
to face off against those fearsome powers.

16:57.130 --> 16:58.860
Are you prepared to handle that?

16:58.860 --> 17:00.370
I can't say I am.

17:00.370 --> 17:02.470
Don't move! Stay still!

17:04.580 --> 17:06.090
"Where's my cap?"

17:06.090 --> 17:08.600
"It'll affect the post office 
with chapped hands."

17:08.600 --> 17:11.490
"Consult a tiny squeeze of eye drops."

17:11.490 --> 17:14.090
Is it no good without his usual hat?

17:14.090 --> 17:17.840
Further recovery from Pontaro's 
wibble-wobble surgery is impossible, then?

17:17.840 --> 17:19.000
Huh? Hold on.

17:19.000 --> 17:22.890
"If 7G isn't stopped, 
even Ikebukuro will disappear."

17:22.890 --> 17:28.530
"Must find cause of 7G 
and repair broken world."

17:28.530 --> 17:33.850
"Need to ruin Pontaro's future plans 
and put an end to them."

17:33.850 --> 17:34.910
Has he recovered a bit?

17:34.910 --> 17:36.150
Wait a minute.

17:36.150 --> 17:38.080
What do you mean, Ikebukuro will disappear?

17:38.080 --> 17:39.910
"Increase in entropy."

17:39.910 --> 17:42.470
"Miniature version of cosmic expansion."

17:42.470 --> 17:43.480
"The Big Rip."

17:43.480 --> 17:45.200
"The soap bubbles popped."

17:45.200 --> 17:46.900
"They popped, and they're gone."

17:46.900 --> 17:48.790
Forget the theory! When will it disappear?!

17:48.790 --> 17:52.900
"Choo-choo choo-choo-choo..."

17:52.900 --> 17:54.110
"No idea"?!

17:55.620 --> 17:59.100
"It could be tomorrow. It could be 
two billion years from now."

17:59.100 --> 18:00.720
"No one can predict it."

18:01.210 --> 18:02.210
Zenjiro...

18:02.210 --> 18:04.800
I wouldn't expect to hear those 
words out of an engineer.

18:05.460 --> 18:06.990
I get it, I get it!

18:06.990 --> 18:08.230
Whoa, whoa, whoa...

18:08.910 --> 18:12.480
If we can't avoid 
annihilation via expansion...

18:12.480 --> 18:14.950
Why don't you put a stop to your journey?

18:14.950 --> 18:16.680
Yeah! It's too dangerous, hermit!

18:16.680 --> 18:18.280
Don't be ridiculous!

18:18.280 --> 18:21.480
The world continues to change, 
now and in the future!

18:21.480 --> 18:23.290
How could I turn my eyes away?!

18:23.290 --> 18:24.380
How irrational.

18:24.380 --> 18:26.950
Life is all about being irrational!

18:26.950 --> 18:30.220
Did you lead an irrational life before 7G?

18:30.220 --> 18:30.800
Indeed.

18:30.800 --> 18:33.650
To sum it up, it was a big, old, absurd mess!

18:33.650 --> 18:35.510
What did you do in Ikebukuro?

18:35.510 --> 18:38.880
Being grown-up means not 
asking questions like that.

18:39.170 --> 18:41.320
My nugget of wisdom, revised edition!

18:41.320 --> 18:42.460
A new map?

18:42.460 --> 18:43.320
That's right.

18:43.320 --> 18:47.090
If you're headed to Ikebukuro, 
I'm sure it'll be of use.

18:47.090 --> 18:48.600
Then this is thanks for the map.

18:48.600 --> 18:49.310
Take it with you.

18:49.310 --> 18:53.440
We'll probably be able to find more food, 
but I dunno about you.

18:53.440 --> 18:54.110
This as well.

18:54.460 --> 18:57.490
There's no guarantee that it won't 
be cold wherever you end up.

18:58.510 --> 19:00.350
I'll happily accept those.

19:00.350 --> 19:03.300
You say that, but we might suddenly 
run into each other again tomorrow.

19:03.300 --> 19:04.690
That's also possible.

19:04.690 --> 19:07.080
Nothing is certain in this world of ours.

19:07.440 --> 19:08.700
Be careful!

19:08.700 --> 19:10.550
I could say the same to you.

19:10.550 --> 19:10.960
What?

19:10.960 --> 19:15.330
If you think Ikebukuro is safe and bustling 
because of its expansion, you're dead wrong.

19:15.330 --> 19:16.350
It's the complete opposite!

19:16.350 --> 19:17.450
What do you mean?

19:17.450 --> 19:20.850
Its citizens can't escape, 
so they're trapped inside.

19:20.850 --> 19:23.880
I'm out here purely due to a stroke of luck!

19:23.880 --> 19:26.760
The Witch Queen of Ikebukuro 
is like staring into an abyss!

19:26.760 --> 19:28.000
Abyss?

19:28.000 --> 19:31.470
She's made up of mystery, 
fear, and the unknown.

19:31.470 --> 19:34.310
By the Witch of Ikebukuro, 
do you mean Yoka-chan?

19:34.310 --> 19:37.830
That may very well have been 
her name, but I forget!

19:37.830 --> 19:39.640
Yoka would never do anything bad!

19:39.640 --> 19:42.460
People change. As does the world.

19:42.460 --> 19:44.720
Do you know of anything 
that always stays the same?

19:45.730 --> 19:46.700
Sure I do!

19:47.030 --> 19:48.190
I see.

19:48.190 --> 19:51.130
But that only <i>appears</i> to be the same.

19:51.130 --> 19:56.350
Since anything unchanging must always 
be moving to stay where it is...

19:56.350 --> 19:57.330
Exactly.

19:57.330 --> 19:59.720
Nothing is eternal or indestructible.

19:59.720 --> 20:02.270
Why do you have to ruin 
the mood at the very end?

20:02.270 --> 20:03.380
Forget what I said, then!

20:03.380 --> 20:03.940
Not happening!

20:03.940 --> 20:04.890
We already heard you!

20:05.760 --> 20:08.030
I want to learn about the ever-changing,

20:08.030 --> 20:10.470
and you want to restore the indestructible.

20:10.470 --> 20:12.160
That's what makes this interesting!

20:12.400 --> 20:17.240
If I find Nishi-Agano, which lies 
beyond your hometown of Agano,

20:17.240 --> 20:22.160
or if I unexpectedly run into the 
Seibu Shinjuku or Tobu Tojo line,

20:22.160 --> 20:23.950
that's when I'll head back!

20:23.950 --> 20:25.480
With that, fare thee well!

20:25.480 --> 20:27.050
He left with a cool line.

20:27.050 --> 20:29.630
How exactly is he planning to go back?

20:29.630 --> 20:31.290
Who knows...

20:36.060 --> 20:37.110
Kusamochi?

20:37.110 --> 20:38.570
What? Sounds tasty!

20:38.570 --> 20:39.690
What's this one, then?

20:39.690 --> 20:40.360
Curry?

20:40.360 --> 20:41.420
But it's in a bowl.

20:41.420 --> 20:43.310
I can tell he looked into all of this,

20:43.310 --> 20:45.200
but that hermit's drawings 
really aren't great.

20:45.200 --> 20:46.370
I want some kusamochi!

20:46.370 --> 20:47.120
With chunky anko!

20:47.120 --> 20:48.220
What? It's gotta be smooth!

20:48.220 --> 20:49.420
You don't get it.

20:49.420 --> 20:50.890
The real experts like it chunky!

20:50.890 --> 20:53.640
Do you think Yoka-chan is doing okay?

20:55.440 --> 20:56.840
I'm sure she is.

20:56.840 --> 20:59.100
I'm worried, since something 
seemed off about her.

20:59.100 --> 21:02.430
In the photo, she looked 
completely different.

21:02.690 --> 21:05.610
I wonder why they're calling her 
the Witch of Ikebukuro.

21:05.610 --> 21:09.580
I think it must be some sort of 
mix-up or mistake. Gotta be!

21:09.580 --> 21:10.260
Yeah, totally.

21:10.260 --> 21:12.130
Yoka-chan's always been so quiet!

21:12.130 --> 21:13.890
No way she could be the witch!

21:13.890 --> 21:17.870
Maybe Yoka-chan got involved 
with some bad people.

21:28.160 --> 21:29.710
What do you want?

21:29.710 --> 21:31.970
I received a report from Oizumi-gakuen.

21:31.970 --> 21:35.300
There are some annoying pests 
on their way to Ikebukuro.

21:35.300 --> 21:37.270
It seems they know the princess.

21:37.270 --> 21:41.290
It'll be a big problem if she meets her 
old friends and regains her memories.

21:41.290 --> 21:45.320
I've placed Shiinamachi on high alert, 
but we need to be extra careful.

21:45.320 --> 21:47.070
Be prepared to eliminate them.

21:47.070 --> 21:50.220
Your job is to protect the princess.

21:50.220 --> 21:51.420
I know that.

22:01.980 --> 22:04.790
What am I doing?

22:05.400 --> 22:08.760
Why am I in a place like this?
